title: National Revolutionary Army
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: nra_timer <= 0
card-image: img/nationalarmy.jpg
on-arrival: week_actions += 1; nra_timer += 3; nra_militarization_cost = 2 if nra_militancy > 0.1 else nra_militarization_cost = 1; nra_militarization_cost = 3 if nra_militancy > 0.25
#subtitle: Military organizing for the Northern Expedition.

= National Revolutionary Army

The *National Revolutionary Army* is the Guomindang's military wing. It is still in it's infancy but is quickly expanding in quality and size.

- @militant: Fund more military-style training and equipment for the NRA.
- @militant_2: Use our existing funds to support more training for the NRA.
- @increase: Increase conscription.
- @decrease: Decrease conscription.
- @same: Keep the NRA as it is.
- @cut_nra: Cut funding for the NRA.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@militant
choose-if: funds >= nra_militarization_cost
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds ([+ nra_militarization_cost +] needed).
subtitle: -[+ nra_militarization_cost +] funds
on-arrival: funds -= nra_militarization_cost; nra_investment += 1; nra_strength += 10; nra_strength += 10 if conscription > 2; nra_strength += 5 if conscription > 3; nra_militancy += 0.05; 

Increasing the strength of the NRA makes us more prepared for the Northern Expedition.

@militant_2
view-if: funded_nra >= 1
on-arrival: nra_militancy += 0.1; funded_nra -= 1

As we have already funded our government funds towards the National Revolutionary Army, we can invest in building up their militancy.

@increase
choose-if: conscription < 5
unavailable-subtitle: Conscription is way too high.
subtitle: +10 thousand
on-arrival: nra_strength += 10; conscription += 1; rural_kmt -= 10;

Increasing conscription is pretty unpopular with the people.

@decrease
choose-if: conscription > 1
unavailable-subtitle: Conscription is already way too low.
subtitle: -10 thousand
on-arrival: nra_strength -= 10; conscription -= 1; rural_kmt += 5;

Decreasing conscription is more popular with the people, although it reduces the NRA's numbers.

@same

The National Revolutionary Army is already serving the purpose it needs to serve. There is no reason to change what already works.

- @return: Continue...


@cut_nra
subtitle: +1 funds
on-arrival: funds += 1; nra_strength -= 10; nra_militancy -= 0.02; left_strength -= 2; left_dissent += 2; red_militancy += 0.05; workers_cpc += 2; unemployed_cpc += 2

Cutting our funds to the National Revolutionary Army causes a drop in the membership, and leads some would-be members to join the Communists instead.
